Test graphs

make check runs the explicit WQH method in graphswitching and the original
gen_all_srgs_wqh_generic program for every entry in cases.txt, then requires
their output to be byte-for-byte identical. It also compares the default GM
method with gen_all_srgs on Sp(6,2), and checks automatic order detection,
n=... headers, file input/output, help, and version reporting.
generate_algebraic_fixtures.py independently reconstructs the named
symplectic, bilinear forms, generalized-quadrangle, and paper benchmark
graphs. It checks their stored matrices and either their strongly regular
parameters or their exact order and degree set.

check_fixed_methods.py verifies the rational orthogonality and irreducible
subgraph counts for every fixed Simoens--Van Overberghe catalogue, then
exercises a guaranteed nontrivial ordinary switch for every method. Under
make check-symmetry, it also requires ordinary and --sym enumeration to
produce the same nonempty canonical class set on those examples.

test_graphswitching_explore.py checks graph6 decoding, adjacency-matrix
conversion, automorphism bounds, canonical seed handling, per-round
deduplication, graph limits, parallel worker pipelines, and optional
automorphism-size filtering. It uses deterministic stand-in commands, so
the default make check does not require nauty gtools.

When graphswitching has nauty support and the nauty gtools are available,
make check-symmetry checks GM --sym on Petersen, Clebsch, GQ(2,4), and
Sp(6,2); WQH --sym on Sp(6,2), GQ(2,4), Bil(2,2,3), and Sp(4,4) is checked
as well. The order-8 and asymmetric Sp(6,2) descendants are also included.
Each output is canonically labelled and required to contain the same
expected isomorphism classes as the complete enumeration. This check
intentionally does not require byte-for-byte output agreement.

The paper fixtures reconstruct the nine graph families in Table 2 of the
Simoens--Van Overberghe preprint: Cycle(20), a seeded G(20,1/2), Brinkmann,
Complete(30), VO-(6,2), Kneser(9,3), Grassmann J_2(5,2), and Hamming(4,6),
together with the existing Sp(6,2) fixture. The paper does not specify its
random seed, so the fixture fixes seed 0.

The fixtures use the following deterministic vertex orderings.

cycle4
    Parameters: 4 vertices, p=1
    Construction: Vertices in cyclic order.
    Test purpose: Small switching and output smoke test.

petersen
    Parameters: 10 vertices, p=2
    Construction: The 2-subsets of {0,...,4} in lexicographic order;
    disjoint subsets are adjacent.
    Test purpose: Small nontrivial strongly regular graph.

clebsch
    Parameters: 16 vertices, p=2
    Construction: Four-bit words in numeric order; words at Hamming
    distance 1 or 4 are adjacent.
    Test purpose: Medium switching and output test.

generalized-quadrangle-gq2-4
    Parameters: SRG(27,10,1,5), p=5
    Construction: Nonzero singular vectors of the elliptic quadratic form
    on GF(2)^6, in numeric order; orthogonal points are adjacent.
    Test purpose: Small output-producing test for WQH 5,5,n-10.

symplectic-sp6-2
    Parameters: SRG(63,30,13,15), p=3
    Construction: Nonzero vectors of GF(2)^6 in numeric order; distinct
    vectors are adjacent when their standard symplectic product is 0.
    Test purpose: Sp(6,2) comparison and a tuple-enumeration-heavy test.

symplectic-sp6-2-gm2-aut8
    Parameters: 63 vertices, automorphism group order 8.
    Construction: Canonical representative reached after two rounds of GM
    switching from symplectic-sp6-2.
    Test purpose: Symmetry-overhead benchmark near the observed crossover.

symplectic-sp6-2-gm3-aut1
    Parameters: 63 vertices, trivial automorphism group.
    Construction: Canonical representative reached after three rounds of GM
    switching from symplectic-sp6-2.
    Test purpose: Symmetry-overhead benchmark with no nontrivial symmetry.

paley73
    Parameters: 73 vertices, p=3
    Construction: Residues modulo 73 in numeric order; distinct residues
    are adjacent when their difference is a nonzero square.
    Test purpose: Larger tuple-enumeration-heavy test.

bilinear-forms-bil2-2-3
    Parameters: SRG(81,32,13,12), p=3
    Construction: The 2 by 2 matrices over GF(3) in lexicographic order;
    matrices are adjacent when their difference has rank 1.
    Test purpose: Full benchmark for WQH 3,3,n-6.

symplectic-sp4-4
    Parameters: SRG(85,20,3,5), p=4
    Construction: Projective points of GF(4)^4 in normalized lexicographic
    order; distinct points are adjacent when their standard symplectic
    product is 0.
    Test purpose: Full benchmark for WQH 4,4,n-8.

The Sp(6,2) and Paley(73) p=3 cases emit only the n=... header.
Consequently, their running time primarily exercises candidate-tuple
enumeration instead of matrix output. The two other large fixtures exercise
the one-step switching cases reported for their respective SRG families.

Regenerate the algebraically defined fixtures after intentionally changing
their construction:

    python3 tests/generate_algebraic_fixtures.py --write
